    {
     "tabId": "ba668641-8b47-5d41-8ac6-af6b7acb6265",
     "collapsed": false,
     "id": "7790e754-c598-5a02-ab02-527d742a784f",
     "gridsterCoords": {
      "w": 12,
      "x": 1,
      "h": 7,
      "y": 22
     },
     "type": "TextDisplay",
     "title": "How to read this",
     "config": {
      "locationUrl": "",
      "locationFile": "",
      "editorData": "<div style=\"font-family:'Metropolis','Segoe UI',sans-serif;font-size:13px;padding:12px 14px;background:#2b3137;color:#e9edf0;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);border-radius:6px\">\n<h2 style=\"font-size:15px;font-weight:700;margin:2px 0 10px 0;color:#e9edf0\">Host resources &mdash; what does vSAN itself consume on each host?</h2>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">This screen shows what vSAN consumes on a host: the memory used by each vSAN daemon, vSAN's CPU figures, and vSAN's network traffic aggregated per host. It does not show the host's total load, which vCenter reports in <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">Host health and load</b> on the Overview screen and <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">Every uplink - from vCenter</b> on the Network screen.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">The CPU table has one row per host. It shows <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">readyPct</code>, <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">usedPct</code> and <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">runPct</code> and the peak run and used percentages, as reported by the vSAN Performance Service.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">The memory table lists the memory consumed and reserved by each vSAN daemon. It reports memory use, not whether a daemon is responding.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">The network table is vSAN's traffic per host, where the Network screen shows the same counters per vmknic.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">Reading any column here</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">A blank cell is not a zero.</b> A blank cell means no value was collected for that column in the selected period.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">Raw columns are cumulative counts.</b> Where a column has a Raw twin, the Raw column is the cumulative count and the other column is a per-interval rate.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">vSAN daemon memory</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN Host Memory</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Kernel consumed size</span> &mdash; Memory in use by the vSAN kernel modules.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Kernel Reserved Memory Size</span> &mdash; Memory reserved for the vSAN kernel modules.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Uw consumed size</span> &mdash; Memory consumed by vSAN user-world processes in total.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">User world Reserved Memory Size</span> &mdash; Memory reserved for vSAN user-world processes.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Clomd consumed size</span> &mdash; Memory used by clomd, the cluster level object manager daemon.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Clomd reserved size</span> &mdash; Memory reserved for clomd.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Cmmdsd consumed size</span> &mdash; Memory used by <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">cmmdsd</b>, the cluster directory service that maintains membership and object metadata.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Cmmdsd reserved size</span> &mdash; Memory reserved for cmmdsd.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Vsanmgmtd consumed size</span> &mdash; Memory used by vsanmgmtd, the vSAN management daemon.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Epd consumed size</span> &mdash; Memory used by epd, a vSAN daemon.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Osfsd consumed size</span> &mdash; Memory used by osfsd, the object filesystem daemon.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Vsandevicemonitord consumed size</span> &mdash; Memory used by vsandevicemonitord, the vSAN device monitor daemon.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">vSAN CPU - is it starved?</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN Host CPU</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Percentage of Ready CPU Time</span> &mdash; Percentage of ready CPU time for vSAN's threads: time they were ready to run but had not been given a physical CPU. Reported by the vSAN Performance Service.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Run % (max)</span> &mdash; Highest running-CPU percentage for vSAN in the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Percentage of Used CPU Time</span> &mdash; Percentage of used CPU time for vSAN, as reported by the vSAN Performance Service.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Percentage of Running CPU Time</span> &mdash; Percentage of running CPU time for vSAN, as reported by the vSAN Performance Service.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Used % (max)</span> &mdash; Highest used-CPU percentage for vSAN in the interval.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">Host network - all vSAN</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN Host Network</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Network In Packet Discard Rate</span> &mdash; Proportion of inbound packets discarded at the host network layer, across all of this host's vSAN traffic rather than one uplink.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Network Out Packet Discard Rate</span> &mdash; Proportion of outbound packets discarded at the host network layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">In Packet Drop Rate (host port)</span> &mdash; Inbound packets dropped by the vSwitch for this port.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Out Packet Drop Rate (host port)</span> &mdash; The vSwitch discarded outbound packets for this port.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Network In Throughput</span> &mdash; Inbound throughput for this host's vSAN traffic. Context for the error columns.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Network Out Throughput</span> &mdash; Outbound throughput for this host's vSAN traffic.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Network In Packets Per Second</span> &mdash; Inbound packets per second.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Network Out Packets Per Second</span> &mdash; Outbound packets per second.</p>\n</div>\n",
